+Write the skill in the consuming project's own skill source, not the shared PSTACK bundle or a generated installation. Follow the project's skill-authoring guidance; for Skillbox, load `skillbox skills get skillbox-author`. Give it frontmatter that names the area and says when to use it. Without frontmatter, the skill never registers. From the skill alone, the next agent must be able to tell whether a change touches the verified code, run the check, tell a real bug from a modeling error, and update the verification when a change is intended. Put the coverage record and the sync commit in the skill, and tell the next agent to move the sync commit forward only after it confirms that the verification describes the code at the new commit. Use this repo's real commands, paths, and nouns, and leave no placeholders.
 
